1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,600
What if you invested
just ₹10,000 every year

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:07,570
in the Nifty 50?
Let's find out.

3
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:09,600
The year is 2006.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,370
You put in your
first ₹10,000.

5
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:13,180
The market surges
nearly 40 percent,

6
00:00:13,530 --> 00:00:14,800
growing it to
almost ₹14,000.

7
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,900
2007 is even better.

8
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,520
A massive 55% rally pushes
your portfolio past ₹37,000.

9
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:19,210
Then 2008 hits.

10
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:22,390
The Global Financial Crisis
wipes out over 50 percent.

11
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:24,030
Your ₹30,000 invested?
Now just ₹22,000.

12
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,420
But you don't stop.

13
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,400
2009 brings an incredible
76% bounce.

14
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,960
Your portfolio jumps
to ₹57,000.

15
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,200
By 2014, steady growth takes
you past ₹1,66,000

16
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,930
with just ₹90,000 invested.

17
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,840
This is the power
of compounding.

18
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:42,100
Even through the
COVID crash of 2020,

19
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,950
your portfolio
keeps climbing.

20
00:00:44,310 --> 00:00:48,110
By 2021, you've crossed
₹4,70,000.

21
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,500
So let's break it down.

22
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,500
You invested a total
of ₹2,00,000.

23
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,400
Your portfolio grew to
₹7,61,000.

24
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,280
That's ₹5,61,000
in profit.

25
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:58,500
Now think about inflation.

26
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,800
In 2006, a movie ticket
was ₹50.

27
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:00,830
Petrol was ₹47 a litre.
Gold was ₹8,600 for 10g.

28
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,400
Today, movie tickets
cost ₹350.

29
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:05,560
Petrol crosses ₹100.
Gold is over ₹90,000.

30
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:06,500
Your money needs to grow
just to keep up,

31
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:07,070
and the Nifty 50 delivered.

32
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,600
After twenty years,

33
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,770
₹2 lakh became ₹7,61,000.

34
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,800
A 3.8× multiplier.

35
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,340
Even after inflation, you beat
every savings account and FD.

36
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:17,500
Start early.

37
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,300
Stay consistent.

38
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,050
Let time do
the heavy lifting.

